{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Its aftergrowth</b> — two times in the Masorah: one is this, and the other: \"its aftergrowth the dust of the earth\" (Isaiah). And that is what is stated in the Tosefta of Shevi'it: a person breaks through his vineyard and dismantles his fence. And that is what is written: \"stones he ground, waters wash away\" — \"its aftergrowth the dust of the earth\" — that even if it has a fence of stones, he grinds it; and even if floodwaters came upon his field, he does not fence it." "<b>Its untrimmed vines</b> — two times in the Masorah: one is this, and the other: \"its untrimmed vines from snow\" — hint of סחור סחור, they say to the nazirite: to the vineyard do not approach; \"its untrimmed vines\" — that you shall not prune its untrimmed vines. Seventy sabbatical years and jubilees Israel abandoned in the land, and corresponding to them they were exiled seventy years. And this is: \"and she shall be impure two weeks as in her menstruation.\" Seventy is written defective, and written after it: \"as in her menstruation\" — thus they were like a menstruant, as written: \"round about her adversaries Jerusalem was as a menstruant among them\" — like the numerical value of נדה, which is 50. And the first alef of שנה is counted as a year."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "The last sentence reads 'the alef of שנה האחרון' — possibly referring to the plene/defective spelling of שנה; the syntax is terse and the reference uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:35.174646077Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}